Include <cstdint> in featuremaptest.cpp.

WHY: run 53 configured graphite2 successfully and then failed at `ninja`,
rc=1 after four seconds, with every error inside this one file:

    tests/featuremap/featuremaptest.cpp:49:15:
        error: 'uint8_t' was not declared in this scope
    tests/featuremap/featuremaptest.cpp:310:14:
        error: 'uint16_t' was not declared in this scope

and gcc said what to do about it:

    note: 'uint16_t' is defined in header '<cstdint>'; this is probably
          fixable by adding '#include <cstdint>'

Every other error in the log -- the invalid template arguments at 49:22, the
`request for member 'data'`, the `no match for 'operator='` and the pages of
std::pair candidate notes -- CASCADES FROM THOSE TWO. `std::vector<uint8_t>`
cannot be instantiated when uint8_t is not a type, so every later use of that
vector is an error about the wrong thing. Fourteen distinct error lines, one
missing header.

WHY IT COMPILED FOR UPSTREAM AND NOT HERE: graphite2 1.3.14 is from 2018 and
was written against a libstdc++ that pulled <cstdint> in transitively through
<string> or <vector>. Later releases tightened those headers, so code that
never included it directly stopped compiling. This is the same class as the
gcc 4.7 backport in the bridge: old source, newer toolchain, a header that
used to arrive by accident.

WHY PATCH RATHER THAN SKIP THE TESTS: `add_subdirectory(tests)` is
unconditional in graphite2's CMakeLists and there is no option to disable it,
so the alternative is patching the build description to drop a whole
subdirectory. This is one line, it is what upstream's own compiler told us to
write, and it leaves the tree otherwise identical to the tarball. Nothing in
src/ failed -- the library itself builds clean.

The test binaries are built and never run; `veron` runs no upstream suite.
They are not installed, so they do not reach the manifest or the image.

--- a/tests/featuremap/featuremaptest.cpp
+++ b/tests/featuremap/featuremaptest.cpp
@@ -22,5 +22,6 @@
 #include <cassert>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <map>
